{"name":"Merman","hex":"#70859b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"merman","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A legendary creature, human male from the waist up, fishlike from the waist down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/merman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Merman","blocks":[{"text":"A merman, the male counterpart of the mythical female mermaid, is a legendary creature which is human from the waist up and fish-like from the waist down, but may assume normal human shape. Sometimes mermen are described as hideous and other times as handsome."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0a/A_Crowned_Merman_-_Arthur_Rackham.jpg/330px-A_Crowned_Merman_-_Arthur_Rackham.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merman","wikidata":"Q4995044"},{"title":"Merman (horse)","blocks":[{"text":"Merman  (1892–1914) was a Thoroughbred racehorse, one of the finest racehorses in Colonial Australian racing history that raced in Europe. He won at distances from 5 furlongs to 21⁄2 miles. In 2016 Merman was inducted to the Australian Racing Hall of Fame."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Merman-%28Lily-Langtree-horse%29.png/330px-Merman-%28Lily-Langtree-horse%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Merman_(horse)","wikidata":"Q25171953"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gal%C3%A9ria_mesta_Bratislavy11.jpg/500px-Gal%C3%A9ria_mesta_Bratislavy11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gal%C3%A9ria_mesta_Bratislavy11.jpg/1280px-Gal%C3%A9ria_mesta_Bratislavy11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/20/Gal%C3%A9ria_me